@startuml
title P2 Air Rooms - Lifecycle, Alias, and Leave Flow

skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor "Primary A" as A
actor "Primary B" as B
participant "Air lifecycle service" as Service
database "Store" as Store
participant "Runtime resolver" as Runtime
participant "A/B/C Pulsars" as Nodes

== Startup migration ==
A -> Service : boot / first Air-aware action
Service -> Store : backfill active links -> two-member Airs
Store --> Service : stable air_id + memberships

note right of Service
  /approach remains a compatibility alias.
  It now creates or joins a two-member Air
  instead of mutating a long-lived link session.
end note

== Create and join ==
A -> Service : create Air + invite
Service -> Store : insert air, invite, owner membership
Store --> Service : air_id, invite code
Service --> A : invite code + pending state

B -> Service : consume invite / request join
Service -> Store : add pending member
Store --> Service : pending membership
Service --> B : waiting for local confirm

B -> Service : confirm join
Service -> Store : mark member active\nset active Air for B
Service -> Runtime : activate air_id\nbuild peer union
Runtime -> Nodes : shared session key = air_id
Service --> A : Air active
Service --> B : Air active

== Leave / apart ==
B -> Service : leave current Air\n(or /apart alias)
Service -> Store : mark B left\nclear B active-air pointer
Service -> Runtime : detach B only
Runtime -> Nodes : stop/fade B
Runtime -> Nodes : A + C continue\nshared playback
Service --> B : personal orbit restored
Service --> A : Air continues if >= 2 barycenters remain

alt fewer than two barycenters remain
  Service -> Store : mark Air parked
  Service -> Runtime : park shared session\nkeep personal state intact
end

@enduml
